course: dictionary
lesson: 2408
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The right meaning depends on the context, which means the words and sentences around the word. In «A cute puppy wags its tail at everyone», cute means pretty and lovable in a way that makes you smile.
explain: Read the sentence before you choose a meaning. «Don't get cute with me» is not about looks at all. Here cute means clever in a cheeky, annoying way, so the speaker is warning someone not to be sly. Always ask: which meaning would fit in this sentence?
explain: Little words can change the meaning too. «Aw, he's pure cute» uses pure to mean really, so the speaker is saying he is really lovable. Lily says she does not find the ponytail tugging cute, because she finds it annoying. Swap your meaning in and check that it makes sense.
fact: Context decides which meaning of a word is right.
fact: «Cute» means pretty and lovable in a way that makes you smile.
fact: In American English, «cute» can mean attractive.
fact: «Cute» can also mean clever in a cheeky or annoying way, as in «don't get cute with me».
fact: «Pure» in «pure cute» means really.
exercise: «The cute puppy wagged its tail at everyone.» What does cute mean here? | Old and tired | *Pretty and lovable, in a way that makes you smile | Clever in a cheeky way | Very angry
exercise: Ruby says, «Don't get cute with me.» What does cute mean here? | Being pretty | *Clever in a cheeky, annoying way | Sitting very still | Being kind to animals
exercise: «Aw, he's pure cute.» What does pure mean in this sentence? | *Really | Made of gold | Very slowly | Clean and spotless
test: In «Lily does not find the ponytail tugging cute», what is Lily saying? | *The tugging is not lovable; it is annoying | The tugging makes her smile | The tugging is the cutest thing ever | The tugging is like a puppy
test: «The right pet fits the home and the family's life, not just a cute video.» What does cute video suggest? | A video that is boring | A video about maths | *A video that looks sweet and appealing, but may not show what owning a pet is really like | A video that is very long
exam: The article says a cute puppy becomes a big dog that needs walks, food and love for ten years or more. What is the main point? | Dogs should never be bought | *A pet is for life, so a cute puppy is a big commitment | Puppies are always easy to look after | Walks are boring
